    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-73-2-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), and without limitation, the victim will be exploited by a person (the exploiter) if either of the following applies:  (a) the exploiter’s conduct causes the victim to enter into slavery, forced labour or sexual servitude;  (b) the exploiter’s conduct causes an organ of the victim to be removed and:  (i) neither the victim nor the victim’s legal guardian consented to the removal of the organ; and  (ii) the organ was not removed to meet a medical or therapeutic need of the victim." ;
    skos:definition "(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), and without limitation, the victim will be exploited by a person (the exploiter) if either of the following applies:  (a) the exploiter’s conduct causes the victim to enter into slavery, forced labour or sexual servitude;  (b) the exploiter’s conduct causes an organ of the victim to be removed and:  (i) neither the victim nor the victim’s legal guardian consented to the removal of the organ; and  (ii) the organ was not removed to meet a medical or therapeutic need of the victim."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a30631df1d9f7d237658ac8b0aa04ead63b9e53f75beadea7b1a3c68014abfb0" ;
    values:partOf concept:c2004a01078-sch-1-sec-73-2 ;
    cof:pageNumber "9"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Exploitation of a victim by a person (the exploiter) is prohibited." ;
