concept:c2004a01078-sch-1-sec-73-7 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "73 7  Meaning of false travel or identity document"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-73-7 ;
    values:originalText "(1) For the purposes of this Subdivision, a travel or identity document is a false travel or identity document if, and only if:  (a) the document, or any part of the document:  (i) purports to have been made in the form in which it is made by a person who did not make it in that form; or  (ii) purports to have been made in the form in which it is made on the authority of a person who did not authorise its making in that form; or  (b) the document, or any part of the document:  (i) purports to have been made in the terms in which it is made by a person who did not make it in those terms; or  (ii) purports to have been made in the terms in which it is made on the authority of a person who did not authorise its making in those terms; or  (c) the document, or any part of the document:  (i) purports to have been altered in any respect by a person who did not alter it in that respect; or  (ii) purports to have been altered in any respect on the authority of a person who did not authorise its alteration in that respect; or  (d) the document, or any part of the document:  (i) purports to have been made or altered by a person who did not exist; or  (ii) purports to have been made or altered on the authority of a person who did not exist; or  (e) the document, or any part of the document, purports to have been made or altered on a date on which, at a time at which, at a place at which, or otherwise in circumstances in which, it was not made or altered.  (2) For the purposes of this Subdivision, a person is taken to make a false travel or identity document if the person alters a document so as to make it a false travel or identity document (whether or not it was already a false travel or identity document before the alteration).  (3) This section has effect as if a document that purports to be a true copy of another document were the original document.  People smuggling  Schedule 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (People Smuggling, Firearms Trafficking and Other Measures)" ;
    skos:definition "(1) For the purposes of this Subdivision, a travel or identity document is a false travel or identity document if, and only if:  (a) the document, or any part of the document:  (i) purports to have been made in the form in which it is made by a person who did not make it in that form; or  (ii) purports to have been made in the form in which it is made on the authority of a person who did not authorise its making in that form; or  (b) the document, or any part of the document:  (i) purports to have been made in the terms in which it is made by a person who did not make it in those terms; or  (ii) purports to have been made in the terms in which it is made on the authority of a person who did not authorise its making in those terms; or  (c) the document, or any part of the document:  (i) purports to have been altered in any respect by a person who did not alter it in that respect; or  (ii) purports to have been altered in any respect on the authority of a person who did not authorise its alteration in that respect; or  (d) the document, or any part of the document:  (i) purports to have been made or altered by a person who did not exist; or  (ii) purports to have been made or altered on the authority of a person who did not exist; or  (e) the document, or any part of the document, purports to have been made or altered on a date on which, at a time at which, at a place at which, or otherwise in circumstances in which, it was not made or altered.  (2) For the purposes of this Subdivision, a person is taken to make a false travel or identity document if the person alters a document so as to make it a false travel or identity document (whether or not it was already a false travel or identity document before the alteration).  (3) This section has effect as if a document that purports to be a true copy of another document were the original document.  People smuggling  Schedule 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (People Smuggling, Firearms Trafficking and Other Measures)"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "32c55a42ee511885a0ac063d66fb521997f04503e294c3ccbc9fafbf43c5fbc4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "12"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:c2004a01078-sch-1-sec-73-7-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:c2004a01078-sch-1-sec-73-7-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:c2004a01078-sch-1-sec-73-7-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <c2004a01078.pdf> ;
    dc:source "c2004a01078.pdf, p.12" .
