    skos:definition "(1) For the purposes of this Subdivision, a travel or identity document is a false travel or identity document if, and only if:  (a) the document, or any part of the document:  (i) purports to have been made in the form in which it is made by a person who did not make it in that form; or  (ii) purports to have been made in the form in which it is made on the authority of a person who did not authorise its making in that form; or  (b) the document, or any part of the document:  (i) purports to have been made in the terms in which it is made by a person who did not make it in those terms; or  (ii) purports to have been made in the terms in which it is made on the authority of a person who did not authorise its making in those terms; or  (c) the document, or any part of the document:  (i) purports to have been altered in any respect by a person who did not alter it in that respect; or  (ii) purports to have been altered in any respect on the authority of a person who did not authorise its alteration in that respect; or  (d) the document, or any part of the document:  (i) purports to have been made or altered by a person who did not exist; or  (ii) purports to have been made or altered on the authority of a person who did not exist; or  (e) the document, or any part of the document, purports to have been made or altered on a date on which, at a time at which, at a place at which, or otherwise in circumstances in which, it was not made or altered."@en ;
